var FT={"Cruel":{"cat":"G","hb":"TDCSR","d":"Cruelty dice equal to your Proficiency Bonus (d6): extra damage, temporary HP on a crit, or a bonus to Intimidation.","full":"You gain cruelty dice, a number equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and they are d6s. You can spend only one per turn.\n**Extra damage.** When you damage a creature, spend one to add its roll to the damage.\n**Crit rewards.** When you score a critical hit, spend one to gain temporary HP equal to the roll.\n**Intimidation.** When you make a Charisma (Intimidation) check, spend one and add the roll.\nYou regain all spent dice on a rest."},"Flash Recall":{"cat":"G","hb":"TDCSR","d":"Bonus Action: swap a prepared spell for another spell you could prepare, of a level you have slots for. Once per rest.","full":"You must be a spellcaster who prepares spells. As a Bonus Action, prepare a spell of level 1 or higher from your spellbook (Wizard) or your class list (other classes). It must be a level you have slots for, and it replaces a prepared spell of the same or higher level. Rest to use it again.","pre":"Spellcasting"},"Mystic Conflux":{"cat":"G","hb":"TDCSR","d":"Attune to up to four magic items. Cast Identify once per rest without a slot or components.","full":"You attune to up to four magic items at once instead of three, and you can cast Identify without a spell slot or material components. Rest to cast it again this way.","fx":{"notes":[["Note","Mystic Conflux: attune to up to four magic items"]]}},"Remarkable Recovery":{"cat":"G","hb":"TDCSR","d":"Gain HP equal to your Constitution modifier when stabilized, and add it to all healing you receive.","full":"Increase your Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20. When you are stabilized while dying, you regain HP equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Whenever a spell, potion or class feature heals you (not this feat), you regain extra HP equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum 1).","asi":["CON"],"fx":{"notes":[["Note","Remarkable Recovery: healing you receive adds your Constitution modifier (min 1)"]]}},"Spelldriver":{"cat":"G","hb":"TDCSR","d":"Cast a spell as a Bonus Action and another spell with your action, but only one of the two may be level 3 or higher.","full":"When you cast a spell of level 1 or higher as a Bonus Action, you can also use your action to cast another spell of level 1 or higher. If you cast two or more spells in one turn, only one of them can be level 3 or higher.","pre":"Level 11+, Spellcasting"},"Thrown Arms Master":{"cat":"G","hb":"TDCSR","d":"Melee weapons gain the Thrown property, thrown ranges grow, and light thrown weapons return after a miss.","full":"Increase Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20. Simple and martial melee weapons without Thrown gain it for you: one-handed ones have range 20/60 ft, two-handed ones 15/30 ft. Weapons that already have Thrown get +20 ft normal and +40 ft long range. When you miss with a light thrown weapon, it returns to your hand at the end of your turn, and you can catch and stow as many as you threw.","asi":["STR","DEX"]},"Vital Sacrifice":{"cat":"G","hb":"TDCSR","d":"Bonus Action: take 1d6 Necrotic damage for a blood boon (1 hour) that adds 1d6 to an attack, 2d6 Necrotic to a hit, or a d4 penalty to a save.","full":"As a Bonus Action, take 1d6 Necrotic damage (cannot be reduced) to gain a blood boon that lasts 1 hour or until spent. Spend it for one effect: add 1d6 to an attack roll, deal an extra 2d6 Necrotic damage on a hit with an attack or spell, or roll a d4 and subtract it from the save of a creature you force to make a Strength, Dexterity or Constitution save."}};
